on</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Somasundaram</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cytotoxic T-cell memory without antigen</article-title><source>Nat</source><volume>369</volume><fpage>648</fpage><lpage>652</lpage><year>1994</year></citation></ref><ref id="R29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Matloubian</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Concepcion</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CD4+ T cells are required to sustain CD8+ cytotoxic T-cell responses during chronic viral infection</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>68</volume><fpage>8056</fpage><lpage>63</lpage><year>1994</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7966595</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaech</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hemby</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kersh</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahmed</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular and Functional Profiling of Memory CD8 T Cell Differentiation</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>111</volume><fpage>837</fpage><lpage>851</lpage><year>2002</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12526810</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R31"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wherry</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Lineage relationship and protective immunity of memory CD8 T cell subsets</article-title><source>Nat Immunol</source><volume>4</volume><fpage>225</fpage><lpage